course: dictionary
lesson: 13980
title: A box that keeps things safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lockbox is a small box with a lock. People use it to keep things safe, like money, papers or a spare key. «Mum put the spare key in the lockbox by the back door.» The word box tells you it is a container, and lock tells you it can be closed so only some people can open it.
explain: Some lockboxes open with a number code instead of a key. «The cleaner used the code to open the lockbox and find the house key.» The clue is the code: the cleaner had to punch in numbers to get the key out. Ask yourself what the code is for, and you will know how the lockbox works.
explain: Look for clues in the words around the word. «Grandma keeps her important papers in a small lockbox» tells you the lockbox is small, and that it is for things that must stay safe. If you swap in a locked box for a safe, the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A lockbox is a small box with a lock.
fact: People use a lockbox to keep money, papers or valuables safe.
fact: Some lockboxes hold a key, and you open them with a number code.
fact: «Lockbox» can also mean a special bank service in the US, where payments are sent to a secure address.
fact: «Lockbox» is a noun, and the plural is «lockboxes».
exercise: «The spare key was in the lockbox by the door.» What is a lockbox? | A kind of bicycle lock | A cupboard full of toys | A wooden box for growing plants | *A small locked box that keeps things safe
exercise: «The cleaner used the code to open the lockbox.» What did she need the code for? | To make the lockbox heavier | To post a letter | To paint the lockbox blue | *To open the lockbox
exercise: «Grandma keeps her papers safe in a small lockbox.» Find and copy the word that names the box. | *lockbox | safe | papers | keeps
test: «Mum said, "Put the spare key in the lockbox, not under the mat."» Why is a lockbox better than under the mat? | It is bigger than a mat | It stops the rain | *It keeps the key hidden and safe | It makes a loud noise when you open it
test: The holiday rental has a key lockbox by the front door. What does a key lockbox hold? | *A key, which you open with a code | A pair of shoes | A plant | A bicycle
exam: «The holiday rental had a key lockbox by the front door, so guests could get in with the code.» What does key lockbox suggest? | *A small box that holds a key and opens with a code | A type of key ring | A kind of window | A large wooden door
